Shoals.Curves.bootstrap_multi_curve: times_template must have one entry per instrument (the declared YieldCurve extent comes from the template): template has 3 entries for 2 instruments

`times_template` is the only source of the type-level `n` in the result, and
the body never read it, so the declared extent was whatever the caller passed.
Two instruments against a three-wide template returned a value declared
`YieldCurve[3]` carrying two pillars: `rate_at(c, 2.0)` answered 0.043088913 —
correct for the two real pillars, which is why the defect was silent — while
the declared third pillar gave `index 2 out of bounds for list of len 2`.
